IMPORT prelude

-- Computer Misuse Act 1993 (Singapore) -- what counts as access, authority and damage (s 2), the offences a person most meets
-- (ss 3, 4, 5, 7, 8, 8A, 8B, 9, 10), participation (s 12), the most a conviction can cost (ss 3 to 11), how far the Act reaches
-- (s 13), amalgamated charges (s 14), composition (s 16), compensation (s 17) and arrest without warrant (s 19).
--
-- SEAT: the accused person -- an individual whose conduct with a computer, a password or a Singpass credential is in question.
-- Every decision is phrased as that person would ask it.
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation, version in force from 30/12/2025, as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/CMA1993.txt (amendments to Act 21 of 2025, in force 30 December 2025).
--
-- NOT ENCODED. The elements of s 6 (use or interception of a computer service) -- its punishment is encoded. ss 1, 15, 18 and 20
-- (title, the courts' jurisdiction, the saving for investigations, amendment of the Schedules: machinery). s 14(4) (what a charge
-- must say). s 17(3) (recovery as a civil debt). The text in force before 30 December 2025 is not deposited, so conduct before that
-- date gets `not covered by this encoding` from the punishment rule. Regulations prescribing compoundable offences (s 16(2)), a
-- different damage threshold (s 2(1) "damage" (a)) or excluded devices (s 2(1) "computer" (d)) are not deposited: they are inputs.
-- The Act lays prohibitions on the individual, not duties with deadlines, so no regulative rule is written.
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Written straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill, from the seat of the individual to
-- whom the law is applied, with the design defaults ruled on 2026-10-18. No pipeline, no coverage table, no independent test pass,
-- no human gate. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Computer Misuse Act 1993 -- offences and punishment`

§§ `2(1) -- computer`

-- s 2(1): "computer" means an electronic, magnetic, optical, electrochemical, or other data processing device ... "but does not
-- include -- (a) an automated typewriter or typesetter; (b) a portable hand-held calculator; (c) a similar device which is
-- non-programmable or which does not contain any data storage facility; or (d) such other device as the Minister may, by
-- notification in the Gazette, prescribe".
-- Gloss: almost any data-processing device is a computer; a typewriter, a calculator and the like are not.
DECLARE Device IS ONE OF
    `a phone, laptop, server or other data processing device`
    `an automated typewriter or typesetter`
    `a portable hand-held calculator`
    `a similar device that is non-programmable or has no data storage`

GIVEN `the device` IS A Device
      `the Minister has prescribed it as excluded` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is it a computer` IF
        NOT `the Minister has prescribed it as excluded`
    AND CONSIDER `the device`
        WHEN `a phone, laptop, server or other data processing device` THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `2(2), (5), (8) -- securing access, without authority, unauthorised modification`

-- s 2(2): a person "secures access" to a program or data if by causing a computer to perform any function the person "(a) alters or
-- erases the program or data; (b) copies or moves it ...; (c) uses it; or (d) causes it to be output from the computer".
-- Gloss: reading, copying, running, changing or deleting it all count.
GIVEN `I altered or erased it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I copied or moved it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I used or ran it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I caused it to be output or displayed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Have I secured access to the program or data` IF
        `I altered or erased it`
    OR  `I copied or moved it`
    OR  `I used or ran it`
    OR  `I caused it to be output or displayed`

-- s 2(5): access is "unauthorised or done without authority" if the person "(a) is not himself or herself entitled to control access
-- of the kind in question ...; and (b) does not have consent to access by him or her of the kind in question ... from any person who
-- is so entitled". Gloss: you need either the right yourself or the say-so of someone who has it.
GIVEN `I am entitled to control access of that kind` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I had consent to that kind of access from someone so entitled` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Was my access without authority` IF
        NOT `I am entitled to control access of that kind`
    AND NOT `I had consent to that kind of access from someone so entitled`

-- s 2(8): a modification is unauthorised if the person "(a) is not himself or herself entitled to determine whether the modification
-- should be made; and (b) does not have consent to the modification from any person who is so entitled".
GIVEN `I am entitled to decide whether to make the modification` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I had consent to the modification from someone so entitled` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Was my modification unauthorised` IF
        NOT `I am entitled to decide whether to make the modification`
    AND NOT `I had consent to the modification from someone so entitled`

§§ `2(1) -- damage`

-- s 2(1): "damage" means, except for the purposes of section 17, any impairment ... that "(a) causes loss aggregating at least
-- $10,000 in value, or such other amount as the Minister may, by notification in the Gazette, prescribe except that any loss incurred
-- or accrued more than one year after the date of the offence in question must not be taken into account; (b) modifies or impairs,
-- or potentially modifies or impairs, the medical examination, diagnosis, treatment or care of one or more persons; (c) causes or
-- threatens physical injury or death to any person; or (d) threatens public health or public safety".
-- Gloss: damage in this Act's sense raises the ceiling; small losses do not count. The caller states only the loss within one year.
-- No prescribed amount is deposited, so it is an input: NOTHING means $10,000 applies.
GIVEN `the loss within one year after the offence` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount the Minister has prescribed, if any` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `it impaired someone's medical examination, diagnosis, treatment or care` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it caused or threatened physical injury or death` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it threatened public health or public safety` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Did my offence cause damage` IF
        `the loss within one year after the offence` AT LEAST `the threshold`
    OR  `it impaired someone's medical examination, diagnosis, treatment or care`
    OR  `it caused or threatened physical injury or death`
    OR  `it threatened public health or public safety`
    WHERE
        `the threshold` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the amount the Minister has prescribed, if any`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN 10000
            WHEN JUST amount THEN amount

§§ `3 -- unauthorised access`

-- s 3(1): "any person who knowingly causes a computer to perform any function for the purpose of securing access without authority to
-- any program or data held in any computer shall be guilty of an offence". (3): it is immaterial that the act is not directed at any
-- particular program, data or computer.
GIVEN `I knowingly caused a computer to perform a function` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I did it to secure access to a program or data` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that access was without authority` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Have I committed the section 3 offence` IF
        `I knowingly caused a computer to perform a function`
    AND `I did it to secure access to a program or data`
    AND `that access was without authority`

§§ `4 -- access with intent to commit an offence`

-- s 4(1): causing a computer to perform any function "for the purpose of securing access to any program or data held in any computer
-- with intent to commit an offence to which this section applies". (2): "an offence involving property, fraud, dishonesty or which
-- causes bodily harm and which is punishable on conviction with imprisonment for a term of not less than 2 years". (4)(a): "it is
-- immaterial whether ... the access ... is authorised or unauthorised".
-- Reading taken (an inference): "punishable ... with imprisonment for a term of not less than 2 years" is read as the intended
-- offence's maximum term being at least 2 years.
GIVEN `I caused a computer to perform a function to secure access` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I intended to commit another offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that offence involves property, fraud, dishonesty or bodily harm` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the most years of prison for that offence` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Have I committed the section 4 offence` IF
        `I caused a computer to perform a function to secure access`
    AND `I intended to commit another offence`
    AND `that offence involves property, fraud, dishonesty or bodily harm`
    AND `the most years of prison for that offence` AT LEAST 2

§§ `5, 7, 8 -- modification, obstruction, disclosing an access code`

-- s 5(1): "any person who does any act which the person knows will cause an unauthorised modification of the contents of any
-- computer". (4): it is immaterial whether the modification is permanent or temporary.
GIVEN `I knew my act would cause a modification of a computer's contents` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the modification was unauthorised` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Have I committed the section 5 offence` IF
        `I knew my act would cause a modification of a computer's contents`
    AND `the modification was unauthorised`

-- s 7(1): "Any person who, knowingly and without authority or lawful excuse -- (a) interferes with, or interrupts or obstructs the
-- lawful use of, a computer; or (b) impedes or prevents access to, or impairs the usefulness or effectiveness of, any program or data".
GIVEN `I acted knowingly` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I had authority or a lawful excuse` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I interfered with or obstructed the lawful use of a computer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I impeded access to, or impaired, a program or data` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Have I committed the section 7 offence` IF
        `I acted knowingly`
    AND NOT `I had authority or a lawful excuse`
    AND (   `I interfered with or obstructed the lawful use of a computer`
         OR `I impeded access to, or impaired, a program or data`)

-- s 8(1): "Any person who, knowingly and without authority, discloses any password, access code or any other means of gaining access
-- ... shall be guilty of an offence if the person did so -- (a) for any wrongful gain; (b) for any unlawful purpose; or (c) knowing
-- that it is likely to cause wrongful loss to any person."
GIVEN `I knowingly disclosed a password or access code without authority` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I did it for wrongful gain` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I did it for an unlawful purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I knew it was likely to cause someone wrongful loss` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Have I committed the section 8 offence` IF
        `I knowingly disclosed a password or access code without authority`
    AND (   `I did it for wrongful gain`
         OR `I did it for an unlawful purpose`
         OR `I knew it was likely to cause someone wrongful loss`)

§§ `8A -- disclosing my own Singpass`

-- First Schedule para 1(1): the "national digital identity service" is "the electronic service known as Singpass"; a "user" is "an
-- individual who has an account registered with" it.
-- s 8A(1): a user "(a) who discloses any password or access code of the user ... or provides any other means of securing access in
-- the identity of the user ...; and (b) who does so knowing, or having reasonable grounds to believe, that the purpose ... is for any
-- person to commit, or to facilitate the commission by any person of, any offence under any written law".
-- (3): the user "is presumed, until the contrary is proved, to have reasonable grounds to believe" that purpose if "(a) the user does
-- the act for any gain ...; (b) ... knowing that it is likely to cause wrongful loss to any person; or (c) ... fails to take
-- reasonable steps to ascertain the identity and physical location of the person to whom [it] is disclosed or provided".
-- (4): "It is not an offence ... if the user ... had reasonable grounds to believe that the purpose ... is to use or access the
-- national digital identity service to carry out a transaction in the identity of the user for a lawful purpose."
-- Judgments for the court are inputs, conditionally phrased.
DECLARE `My Singpass disclosure` HAS
    `I have a Singpass account` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I disclosed my Singpass password or code, or gave another means of access in my identity` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the court finds I knew or had reasonable grounds to believe it was for an offence` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I did it for any gain` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I knew it was likely to cause someone wrongful loss` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I failed to take reasonable steps to find out who and where the recipient was` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the court is satisfied I proved the contrary of the presumption` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I had reasonable grounds to believe it was for a lawful transaction in my identity` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN d IS A `My Singpass disclosure`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the section 8A(3) presumption stand against me` IF
        (   d's `I did it for any gain`
         OR d's `I knew it was likely to cause someone wrongful loss`
         OR d's `I failed to take reasonable steps to find out who and where the recipient was`)
    AND NOT d's `the court is satisfied I proved the contrary of the presumption`

GIVEN d IS A `My Singpass disclosure`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Have I committed the section 8A offence` IF
        d's `I have a Singpass account`
    AND d's `I disclosed my Singpass password or code, or gave another means of access in my identity`
    AND (   d's `the court finds I knew or had reasonable grounds to believe it was for an offence`
         OR `Does the section 8A(3) presumption stand against me` d)
    AND NOT d's `I had reasonable grounds to believe it was for a lawful transaction in my identity`

§§ `8B -- another person's Singpass credential`

-- First Schedule para 1(2): a credential of another person is "a password, access code or biometric identifier of that other person
-- ..., or any application registered with the national digital identity service in the identity of that other person". Para 1(1):
-- "biometric identifier" is an image or video of a user's face captured through Singpass.
DECLARE Item IS ONE OF
    `their Singpass password`
    `their Singpass access code`
    `an image or video of their face captured through Singpass`
    `a Singpass app registered in their identity`
    `some other detail of theirs, such as an identity card number`

GIVEN `the item` IS AN Item
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is it a Singpass credential of another person` IF
    CONSIDER `the item`
    WHEN `some other detail of theirs, such as an identity card number` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- s 8B(1)(a): "obtains or retains any credential of another person". (2): not an offence if obtained or retained "for a purpose that
-- is not" (a) use in committing or facilitating an offence, or (b) supply for that use.
GIVEN `the item` IS AN Item
      `I obtained or retained it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `my purpose was to use it, or pass it on, for an offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Have I committed the section 8B offence by obtaining or retaining` IF
        `Is it a Singpass credential of another person` `the item`
    AND `I obtained or retained it`
    AND `my purpose was to use it, or pass it on, for an offence`

-- s 8B(1)(b): "supplies, offers to supply, transmits or makes available". (3): not an offence if "(a) the person did the act for a
-- purpose other than for the credential ... to be used in committing, or in facilitating the commission of, any offence ...; and
-- (b) the person did not know or have reason to believe that the credential ... will be or is likely to be used" for one.
-- (4): merely providing network access or routing data is not transmitting or making available.
GIVEN `the item` IS AN Item
      `I supplied, offered, transmitted or made it available` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I only provided network access or routing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `my purpose was for it to be used for an offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I knew or had reason to believe it was likely to be used for an offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Have I committed the section 8B offence by supplying` IF
        `Is it a Singpass credential of another person` `the item`
    AND `I supplied, offered, transmitted or made it available`
    AND NOT `I only provided network access or routing`
    AND (   `my purpose was for it to be used for an offence`
         OR `I knew or had reason to believe it was likely to be used for an offence`)

§§ `9 -- hacked personal information`

-- s 9(1): a person "knowing or having reason to believe that any personal information about another person (being an individual) was
-- obtained by an act done in contravention of section 3, 4, 5 or 6 -- (a) obtains or retains the personal information; or (b)
-- supplies, offers to supply, transmits or makes available" it. (2) and (3) carve out the same innocent purposes as s 8B(2), (3);
-- (4) the same network-provider rule. Gloss: personal information (s 9(7)(a)) includes names, addresses, card numbers and passwords.
GIVEN `I knew or had reason to believe it was obtained by hacking under section 3, 4, 5 or 6` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I obtained or retained it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `my purpose was to use it, or pass it on, for an offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Have I committed the section 9 offence by obtaining or retaining` IF
        `I knew or had reason to believe it was obtained by hacking under section 3, 4, 5 or 6`
    AND `I obtained or retained it`
    AND `my purpose was to use it, or pass it on, for an offence`

GIVEN `I knew or had reason to believe it was obtained by hacking under section 3, 4, 5 or 6` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I supplied, offered, transmitted or made it available` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I only provided network access or routing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `my purpose was for it to be used for an offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I knew or had reason to believe it was likely to be used for an offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Have I committed the section 9 offence by supplying` IF
        `I knew or had reason to believe it was obtained by hacking under section 3, 4, 5 or 6`
    AND `I supplied, offered, transmitted or made it available`
    AND NOT `I only provided network access or routing`
    AND (   `my purpose was for it to be used for an offence`
         OR `I knew or had reason to believe it was likely to be used for an offence`)

§§ `10 -- hacking tools and passwords`

-- s 10(1): "(a) obtains or retains any item ... (i) intending to use it to commit, or facilitate the commission of, an offence under
-- section 3, 4, 5, 6 or 7; or (ii) with a view to it being supplied or made available ... for use in" one; or "(b) makes, supplies,
-- offers to supply or makes available ... any item ..., intending it to be used" for one. (2): the items are "(a) any device,
-- including a computer program, that is designed or adapted primarily, or is capable of being used, for the purpose of committing" one
-- of those offences, and "(b) a password, an access code, or similar data by which the whole or any part of a computer is capable of
-- being accessed".
GIVEN `it is a hacking device or program, or a password or access code` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I obtained or retained it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I made, supplied, offered or made it available` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I intended it for an offence under sections 3 to 7, by me or someone I pass it to` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Have I committed the section 10 offence` IF
        `it is a hacking device or program, or a password or access code`
    AND (`I obtained or retained it` OR `I made, supplied, offered or made it available`)
    AND `I intended it for an offence under sections 3 to 7, by me or someone I pass it to`

§§ `12 -- abetment, attempt and preparation`

-- s 12(1): "Any person who abets the commission of or who attempts to commit or does any act preparatory to or in furtherance of the
-- commission of any offence under this Act shall be guilty of that offence and shall be liable on conviction to the punishment
-- provided for the offence." (2): it is immaterial where the act took place.
DECLARE `My part` IS ONE OF
    `I committed it`
    `I abetted it`
    `I attempted it`
    `I did an act preparatory to or in furtherance of it`
    `I took no part`

GIVEN `my part` IS A `My part`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I guilty of the offence itself` IF
    CONSIDER `my part`
    WHEN `I took no part` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `11 -- protected computers`

-- s 11(2): a computer is "protected" if the offender "knew, or ought reasonably to have known, that the computer or program or data is
-- used directly in connection with or necessary for -- (a) the security, defence or international relations of Singapore; (b) the
-- existence or identity of a confidential source of information relating to the enforcement of a criminal law; (c) the provision of
-- services directly related to communications infrastructure, banking and financial services, public utilities, public
-- transportation or public key infrastructure; or (d) the protection of public safety including systems related to essential
-- emergency services such as police, civil defence and medical services".
-- (3): knowledge is "presumed, until the contrary is proved" if "an electronic or other warning [was] exhibited to the accused stating
-- that unauthorised access ... attracts an enhanced penalty under this section".
DECLARE Use IS ONE OF
    `the security, defence or international relations of Singapore`
    `a confidential source for criminal law enforcement`
    `communications, banking and finance, utilities, public transport or public key infrastructure`
    `public safety, including police, civil defence and medical emergency systems`
    `an ordinary business or personal use`

GIVEN `what the computer is used for` IS A Use
      `I knew or ought reasonably to have known of that use` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a warning of the enhanced penalty was exhibited to me` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court is satisfied I proved I did not have that knowledge` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is it a protected computer` IF
        `a listed use`
    AND (   `I knew or ought reasonably to have known of that use`
         OR (    `a warning of the enhanced penalty was exhibited to me`
             AND NOT `the court is satisfied I proved I did not have that knowledge`))
    WHERE
        `a listed use` MEANS
            CONSIDER `what the computer is used for`
            WHEN `an ordinary business or personal use` THEN FALSE
            OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `3 to 11 -- the most a conviction can cost`

-- The offence, as the person would name the charge.
DECLARE Offence IS ONE OF
    `section 3 unauthorised access`
    `section 4 access with intent to commit an offence`
    `section 5 unauthorised modification`
    `section 6 unauthorised use or interception of a computer service`
    `section 7 obstruction of use of a computer`
    `section 8 disclosing an access code`
    `section 8A disclosing my own Singpass`
    `section 8B obtaining or retaining another's Singpass credential`
    `section 8B supplying another's Singpass credential`
    `section 9 dealing in hacked personal information`
    `section 10 hacking tools and passwords`

-- Each section's fine and imprisonment ceilings, first conviction then "second or subsequent conviction". "or to both" throughout.
-- s 3(1): $5,000 / 2 years; $10,000 / 3 years.     s 4(3): $50,000 / 10 years (no repeat limb).
-- ss 5(1), 6(1), 7(1), 8(2), 8B(5), 9(5), 10(3): $10,000 / 3 years; $20,000 / 5 years.
-- s 8A(1): $10,000 / 3 years (no repeat limb).
DECLARE `Penalty row` HAS
    `first fine`     IS A NUMBER
    `first years`    IS A NUMBER
    `repeat fine`    IS A NUMBER
    `repeat years`   IS A NUMBER

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A `Penalty row`
DECIDE `the section's own ceilings for` `the offence` IS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    --                                                                       first fine, years, repeat fine, years
    WHEN `section 3 unauthorised access`                       THEN `Penalty row` OF  5000,  2, 10000,  3
    WHEN `section 4 access with intent to commit an offence`   THEN `Penalty row` OF 50000, 10, 50000, 10
    WHEN `section 8A disclosing my own Singpass`               THEN `Penalty row` OF 10000,  3, 10000,  3
    OTHERWISE                                                       `Penalty row` OF 10000,  3, 20000,  5

-- ss 3(2), 5(2), 6(2), 7(2): "If any damage is caused as a result of an offence under this section, a person convicted of the offence
-- shall be liable to a fine not exceeding $50,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 7 years or to both." s 11(1): where
-- access to a protected computer is obtained in the course of an offence under s 3, 5, 6 or 7, "in lieu of the punishment prescribed
-- in those sections", "a fine not exceeding $100,000 or ... imprisonment for a term not exceeding 20 years or ... both".
GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `has the damage and protected-computer limbs` `the offence` IF
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `section 3 unauthorised access` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `section 5 unauthorised modification` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `section 6 unauthorised use or interception of a computer service` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `section 7 obstruction of use of a computer` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- Caning, up to 12 strokes, in addition to the fine or prison (individuals only; the seat is an individual):
-- s 8A(5): "(a) if the individual knew that the purpose ... was for any person to commit, or to facilitate the commission by any person
-- of, any scam offence; or (b) if -- (i) it is proved, to the satisfaction of the court, that the password ... was used to commit, or
-- to facilitate the commission of, a scam offence; and (ii) the individual is not able to prove, to the satisfaction of the court,
-- that he or she had, at any time, taken reasonable steps to ensure that [it] would not be used" for one.
-- s 8B(5A) (obtaining or retaining): if obtained or retained "(a) for use in committing, or in facilitating the commission of, any scam
-- offence; or (b) for the supply ... [of] the credential to be used in" one.
-- s 8B(5B) (supplying): the same two limbs as s 8A(5), about the credential.
-- Second Schedule: a "scam offence" is an offence under s 420(2) of the Penal Code 1871, or its abetment, conspiracy or attempt.
DECLARE `My sentencing facts` HAS
    `the offence I am convicted of` IS AN Offence
    `my conduct was on or after 30 December 2025` IS A BOOLEAN
    `this is my second or later conviction for it` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the court finds damage was caused` IS A BOOLEAN
    `access to a protected computer was obtained in the course of it` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I knew it was for a scam offence` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I obtained or retained it for a scam offence` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the court is satisfied it was used for a scam offence` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the court is satisfied I proved reasonable steps against scam use` IS A BOOLEAN

-- The answer. Conduct before 30 December 2025 is not covered: only the text in force from that date is deposited.
DECLARE `The most I face` IS ONE OF
    `not covered by this encoding`
    `a fine, prison, or both, and caning`
        HAS `fine up to` IS A NUMBER
            `years of prison up to` IS A NUMBER
            `strokes of the cane up to` IS A NUMBER

GIVEN f IS A `My sentencing facts`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the strokes I can be given` f IS
    CONSIDER f's `the offence I am convicted of`
    WHEN `section 8A disclosing my own Singpass` THEN `the scam limbs`
    WHEN `section 8B supplying another's Singpass credential` THEN `the scam limbs`
    WHEN `section 8B obtaining or retaining another's Singpass credential` THEN
        IF f's `I obtained or retained it for a scam offence` THEN 12 ELSE 0
    OTHERWISE 0
    WHERE
        `the scam limbs` MEANS
            IF     f's `I knew it was for a scam offence`
                OR (    f's `the court is satisfied it was used for a scam offence`
                    AND NOT f's `the court is satisfied I proved reasonable steps against scam use`)
            THEN 12
            ELSE 0

GIVEN f IS A `My sentencing facts`
GIVETH A `The most I face`
DECIDE `What is the most I can be punished with` f IS
    IF NOT f's `my conduct was on or after 30 December 2025`
    THEN `not covered by this encoding`
    ELSE BRANCH
            IF `limbs apply` AND f's `access to a protected computer was obtained in the course of it`
                THEN `a fine, prison, or both, and caning` 100000 20 `strokes`
            IF `limbs apply` AND f's `the court finds damage was caused`
                THEN `a fine, prison, or both, and caning` 50000 7 `strokes`
            IF f's `this is my second or later conviction for it`
                THEN `a fine, prison, or both, and caning` (`row`'s `repeat fine`) (`row`'s `repeat years`) `strokes`
            OTHERWISE `a fine, prison, or both, and caning` (`row`'s `first fine`) (`row`'s `first years`) `strokes`
    WHERE
        `row` MEANS `the section's own ceilings for` (f's `the offence I am convicted of`)
        `limbs apply` MEANS `has the damage and protected-computer limbs` (f's `the offence I am convicted of`)
        `strokes` MEANS `the strokes I can be given` f

§§ `13 -- how far the Act reaches`

-- s 13(1): the Act has effect "whatever the person's nationality or citizenship, outside as well as within Singapore", subject to (3):
-- it applies if "(a) ... the accused was in Singapore at the material time; (b) for the offence in question (being one under section 3,
-- 4, 5, 6, 7 or 8), the computer, program or data was in Singapore at the material time; (c) the offence causes, or creates a
-- significant risk of, serious harm in Singapore; or (d) the offence is one under section 8A(1) or 8B(1)".
-- (4): "serious harm in Singapore" is illness, injury or death of individuals in Singapore; disruption of, or serious loss of public
-- confidence in, an essential service or the Government's functions; or damage to national security, defence or foreign relations.
GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
      `I was in Singapore at the time` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the computer, program or data was in Singapore at the time` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it caused, or created a significant risk of, serious harm in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the Act reach my conduct` IF
        `I was in Singapore at the time`
    OR  (`the computer, program or data was in Singapore at the time` AND `an offence under sections 3 to 8`)
    OR  `it caused, or created a significant risk of, serious harm in Singapore`
    OR  `a Singpass offence`
    WHERE
        `a Singpass offence` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the offence`
            WHEN `section 8A disclosing my own Singpass` THEN TRUE
            WHEN `section 8B obtaining or retaining another's Singpass credential` THEN TRUE
            WHEN `section 8B supplying another's Singpass credential` THEN TRUE
            OTHERWISE FALSE
        `an offence under sections 3 to 8` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the offence`
            WHEN `section 8A disclosing my own Singpass` THEN FALSE
            WHEN `section 8B obtaining or retaining another's Singpass credential` THEN FALSE
            WHEN `section 8B supplying another's Singpass credential` THEN FALSE
            WHEN `section 9 dealing in hacked personal information` THEN FALSE
            WHEN `section 10 hacking tools and passwords` THEN FALSE
            OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `14 -- several acts charged as one`

-- s 14(1): applies when a person "is alleged to have committed 2 or more acts -- (a) each of which is an offence under the same
-- provision in Part 2; (b) that involve the same computer; and (c) that are committed in a period that does not exceed 12 months".
-- (3): "A charge framed in accordance with subsection (2) is treated as a charge of one offence."
GIVEN `the number of acts alleged` IS A NUMBER
      `each is an offence under the same provision` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they involve the same computer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they fall within a period not exceeding 12 months` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can my acts be charged as one offence` IF
        `the number of acts alleged` AT LEAST 2
    AND `each is an offence under the same provision`
    AND `they involve the same computer`
    AND `they fall within a period not exceeding 12 months`

§§ `16 -- composition`

-- s 16(1): the Commissioner of Police or an authorised person "may compound any offence under this Act that is prescribed as a
-- compoundable offence by collecting from a person reasonably suspected of having committed the offence a sum not exceeding $3,000".
-- The regulations under s 16(2) are not deposited: whether the offence is prescribed is an input. Whether to compound is the
-- Commissioner's choice; this answers only the most that can be collected if it is offered. NOTHING: composition is not available.
GIVEN `the offence is prescribed as compoundable` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I am reasonably suspected of it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the most I can be asked to pay to compound` IS
    IF `the offence is prescribed as compoundable` AND `I am reasonably suspected of it`
    THEN JUST 3000
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `17 -- compensation and the civil claim`

-- s 17(1): the court "may make an order against the person for the payment by the person of a sum to be fixed by the court by way of
-- compensation" for damage to another's computer, program or data. (2): a claim for damages "is deemed to have been satisfied to the
-- extent of any amount which has been paid to the person under an order for compensation, but the order does not affect any right to
-- a civil remedy for the recovery of damages beyond the amount of compensation paid".
GIVEN `the damages the victim can prove` IS A NUMBER
      `the compensation I have paid under the order` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much can still be claimed from me in a civil suit` IS
    IF `the damages the victim can prove` GREATER THAN `the compensation I have paid under the order`
    THEN `the damages the victim can prove` MINUS `the compensation I have paid under the order`
    ELSE 0

§§ `19 -- arrest without warrant`

-- s 19: "Any police officer may arrest without warrant any person reasonably suspected of committing an offence under this Act."
GIVEN `the officer reasonably suspects me of an offence under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can a police officer arrest me without a warrant` IF
    `the officer reasonably suspects me of an offence under this Act`
